@@ -59,6 +59,20 @@ Run this command from project root:
 
 <br/>
 
+## Deploy on Wasmer
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-171717?logo=wasmer&logoColor=white)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=sadanandpai%2Ffrontend-mini-challenges)
+
+Wasmer reads the `Anybuild` file in the project root, runs `npm install`, `npm run build` and
+`npm run copy-to-dist`, and serves the assembled site as static files under
+`/frontend-mini-challenges/` (`/` redirects there). The button opens Wasmer's import page for this
+public repository, where you review the detected build settings, correct them if needed, and then
+click Deploy; nothing is deployed until you do. It does not create a copy of the repository in your
+GitHub account. To customize the challenges and redeploy on changes, fork the repository and import
+your fork instead.
+
+<br/>
+
